    "description": "DSD Renewables develops, owns, and operates distributed-energy projects, including solar, storage, EV charging, and community-energy assets. Its counterparties include commercial, industrial, municipal, institutional, and utility customers that contract for distributed-generation output and related services. The business is asset-heavy and contracted because it combines development capability with ownership of operating projects and long-term customer agreements. Company history materials describe DSD as having roots in 2012 and a standalone launch in 2019, after which the platform expanded rapidly and raised more than $1 billion in its first three years. Its operating footprint spans multiple US states, and 2025 financing disclosures referenced 233 MW of solar assets backed by long-term financing. BlackRock has been the platform's majority institutional backer since launch, and Cox Enterprises made a strategic investment in 2023, while public sources do not disclose exact ownership percentages.",
